This tool allows monitoring several values from th following device:
-SOREL LTDC

Other devices may work as well.

For use with Raspberry Pi + MCP2515 Module

Will need to install mosquitto_client and can_utils 

Raspberry Pi Model B (26-Pin Header)
VCC ➡️ Pin 1 (3.3V)
GND ➡️ Pin 6 (GND)
CS ➡️ Pin 24 (GPIO 8 / CE0)
SO ➡️ Pin 21 (GPIO 9 / MISO)
SI ➡️ Pin 19 (GPIO 10 / MOSI)
SCK ➡️ Pin 23 (GPIO 11 / SCLK)
INT ➡️ Pin 22 (GPIO 25)

nano /boot/firmware/config.txt (or /boot/config.txt on older operating systems)

For an 8MHz Board (Most Common):
dtparam=spi=on
dtoverlay=mcp2515-can0,oscillator=8000000,interrupt=25

For a 16MHz Board:
dtparam=spi=on
dtoverlay=mcp2515-can0,oscillator=16000000,interrupt=25

After saving the file, run sudo reboot

Bridge J1 on the MCP2515 board if it is the last device in the can chain
Connect from can port inside LTDC to the MCP2515 can header, left to H, right to L

Check can is discovered
dmesg

Bring up can
ip link set can0 up type can bitrate 250000

Check can interface
ip addr show can0

can-ltdc-logger.c is very close to the original ddimension version
can-ltdc-logger2.c is a heavily modified version by AI to match my LTDC, CAN ID, and publish names to match my existing mqtt values for simplicity with Home Assistant

(I implemented this solution to replace a curl script scraping the Sorel-connect.net nabto page from a Sorel data logger)

Compile 
gcc -o can-ltdc-logger can-ltdc-logger2.c

Test
can-ltdc-logger can0

Can uncomment line 72 for DEBUG 

